# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# The working tree stays native (CRLF on Windows) but everything committed is
# LF. Without this, YAML, SQL and shell files authored on Windows land as CRLF
# and fail `prettier --check`, which runs BEFORE the tests in CI and blocks the
# merge — and shell scripts with CRLF fail at runtime inside a Linux container
# with an error that names the shebang rather than the line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must be LF regardless of any local core.autocrlf setting: these
# are executed by Linux containers.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary, never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
